v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application. v2.1.0-v2.4.0 added the Tie
bet and its own stake, the half-screen layout, PASS recording the table's result, and the OCR
groundwork. v2.5.x-v2.7.x built and proved the OCR tooling, calibration, the confidence gate and the
live loop. v2.8.0 was the milestone: the reader read the user's live casino display. v2.8.1 refused
whole-screen regions. v2.8.2 made the OCR profile follow the session and made drawing start from a
detected table position. v2.8.3 fixed the drawing coordinate conversion, which had been mapping the
user's correct boxes onto the wrong part of the screen.

v2.9.0 shows the capture region live in the OCR panel — the answer to "why is there no result?" — and
fixes the three remaining reasons the live reader produced nothing: a pixel-identical double-read rule
that cancelled every hand on a moving table, an unreadable reply that froze the scan loop forever, and
a gap between reads that straddled the moment a hand settles. A 90-second run of the real reader
against the real screen then recorded BANKER from the live table.

